								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=837.msg8057#msg8057"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=837.msg8057#msg8057">Re: bit of help please</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #7 on:</b> May 21, 2004, 01:05:55 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Kensai. You really think playing EQ again is the best idea ?<br /><br />Unless your wife is a complete psycho, she went after your account because she hates it. <br /><br />I used to have a dog that would get mad at me for not spending enough time with him. He would shit on the floor.<br />He&#039;s dead now, but thats not the point.<br /><br />I had a cat who would scratch up my speakers when he was mad at me. Little bastard learned to fly but he&#039;s not dead yet.<br /><br />John Bobbitt had a wife he didn&#039;t spend enough time with (OK, I&#039;m sugar coating it a bit) and she lopped off his pecker. That bitch got on TV.<br /><br />I guess what I&#039;m saying is that unless you can kill your wife, throw her across the room, or risk getting your ding-a-ling chopped off...you should probably not get back into EQ.<br /><br />Oh...and if by some chance you do, change that INC hotkey.<br />&quot;Tai kwan leap boot to the head&quot; gets old after a while.
